WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.809 --> 00:00:19.073
Sign in as the business owner.

2
00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:24.869
Categories group your products, like Beverages or Dairy. Open Inventory, then Categories.

3
00:00:24.969 --> 00:00:29.179
Each category shows its parent and how many products it holds.

4
00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.730
Click New category to add one.

5
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.004
Give the category a name.

6
00:00:34.104 --> 00:00:39.305
Leave the parent empty for a top level category, or pick one for a sub category.

7
00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:42.846
Add a picture. It is shown on the category card.

8
00:00:42.946 --> 00:00:47.063
Click Save category.

9
00:00:48.364 --> 00:00:54.572
Brands tell customers and reports who makes a product. Open Brands and click New brand.

10
00:00:54.672 --> 00:00:58.921
Type the brand name and save it.

11
00:01:00.222 --> 00:01:07.314
Units say how a product is counted or measured. Open Units and click New unit.

12
00:01:07.414 --> 00:01:12.560
Enter a name and a short name. The short name appears next to prices and stock.

13
00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:17.859
Count is for things you count one by one. Allow decimals only for weighed goods.

14
00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:20.267
Save the unit.

15
00:01:21.568 --> 00:01:27.019
Now use all three on a product. Go to Products and click New product.

16
00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:30.852
Name the product and generate a SKU.

17
00:01:30.952 --> 00:01:33.053
Enter a price.

18
00:01:33.153 --> 00:01:37.970
On the right, the Organization box has your new brand, unit and category.

19
00:01:38.071 --> 00:01:40.252
Choose the unit.

20
00:01:40.352 --> 00:01:42.839
And the category.

21
00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:45.251
Save the product.

22
00:01:46.852 --> 00:01:51.780
The product list now shows the new category and the unit next to the price.

23
00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:59.419
You can also filter the list by any category, brand or unit.

24
00:02:00.722 --> 00:02:05.427
That is how you keep a catalogue tidy. Next, keep an eye on your stock.
